\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Minimal kinematic definitions for Sec.~\ref {sec:water-sail-prop}. In the laboratory frame \(G\), the true wind is \(v_w\) and the boat speed is \(v_b\). In the instantaneous boat frame \(C\), the apparent-wind velocity is \(v_a = v_w - v_b\). Vectors are aligned at a common origin; for \(v_b > v_w\), the apparent-wind velocity \(v_a\) reverses direction.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
